(920866, 105438, 14603, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by PaulMdx:</b></div><hr/><i> I''ve been wondering and wondering which shot was yours, Graham!  Score seems a little low to me, I think it deserved higher than 5.0..  With the kit you had - very nice work. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thanks Paul...I knew that I wouldn`t be scoring highly with this but I had hoped to finish between 5.5 &amp; 6.<br/>It`s a challenge that I probably should have sat out..given the limitations of my set-up and,just as importantly, the opportunities available to me (no daytime soccer).<br/>Out of all the shots I took from the game,(and there were plenty), I thought that this one might do reasonably well since there was an element of humour in it which might help make up for some of the framing deficiences.It also captured an unusual event in that all but one of the opposition players are in the six yard box.<br/>However, I think that most of those elements have been overlooked by the majority of voters,understandably I suppose if you have no knowledge of, or liking for, the sport.</td>', 'Originally posted by PaulMdx: I''ve been wondering and wondering which shot was yours, Graham!  Score seems a little low to me, I think it deserved higher than 5.0..  With the kit you had - very nice work.  Thanks Paul...I knew that I wouldn`t be scoring highly with this but I had hoped to finish between 5.5 & 6.It`s a challenge that I probably should have sat out..given the limitations of my set-up and,just as importantly, the opportunities available to me (no daytime soccer).Out of all the shots I took from the game,(and there were plenty), I thought that this one might do reasonably well since there was an element of humour in it which might help make up for some of the framing deficiences.It also captured an unusual event in that all but one of the opposition players are in the six yard box.However, I think that most of those elements have been overlooked by the majority of voters,understandably I suppose if you have no knowledge of, or liking for, the sport.', '2004-09-22 07:10:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(920897, 105255, 8522, '<td valign="top">Having had a second look, I wonder how this would have looked flipped horizontally. Most people''s eyes (in the west) are used to reading from left to right, and I''m wondering if this would have scored higher with the implied motion following the left-&gt;right path.</td>', 'Having had a second look, I wonder how this would have looked flipped horizontally. Most people''s eyes (in the west) are used to reading from left to right, and I''m wondering if this would have scored higher with the implied motion following the left->right path.', '2004-09-22 08:21:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(920906, 105255, 15029, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by BobsterLobster:</b></div><hr/><i> Having had a second look, I wonder how this would have looked flipped horizontally. Most people''s eyes (in the west) are used to reading from left to right, and I''m wondering if this would have scored higher with the implied motion following the left-&gt;right path. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I thought about that, but since most people kick better with their right foot, kicking across the body to the left side of the goal seems more natural<br/>but I don''t know, maby it would have worked better the other way.</td>', 'Originally posted by BobsterLobster: Having had a second look, I wonder how this would have looked flipped horizontally. Most people''s eyes (in the west) are used to reading from left to right, and I''m wondering if this would have scored higher with the implied motion following the left->right path.   I thought about that, but since most people kick better with their right foot, kicking across the body to the left side of the goal seems more naturalbut I don''t know, maby it would have worked better the other way.', '2004-09-22 08:29:35.000000', NULL, 0),
