(921949, 104630, 7560, '<td valign="top">This was actually one of my top three for this challenge. I loved the emotion that you captured on both players faces. The element that made this shot so strong though was the fact that the player recieving the ball  is looking away from the person about to tackle him. It hightens the anticipation enormously. Well done.</td>', 'This was actually one of my top three for this challenge. I loved the emotion that you captured on both players faces. The element that made this shot so strong though was the fact that the player recieving the ball  is looking away from the person about to tackle him. It hightens the anticipation enormously. Well done.', '2004-09-22 17:36:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(922052, 104495, 15407, '<td valign="top">Hello John, Did you ever determine if that 655 m subject distance comes from using a lens setting of infinity?  Is it a Cannon lens &amp; does it give you accurate readings at subject distance less than Infinity?  Ref: Our comments on ''Gaia''<br/>Tim</td>', 'Hello John, Did you ever determine if that 655 m subject distance comes from using a lens setting of infinity?  Is it a Cannon lens & does it give you accurate readings at subject distance less than Infinity?  Ref: Our comments on ''Gaia''Tim', '2004-09-22 18:35:25.000000', NULL, 0),
